 "observations": [
  "The page number «137» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it; at the right the number of the table, «Tab. 26», in bold sans serif, underlined. The titles (L01, L02), in bold, the sigla in roman, as on p. 133 (JP2 0165); the folios of the manuscripts, «C 55v, O 113r,» over «N 23r.», stand at the right of the titles, the letters raised; here as margin notes. At the foot, the signature line of the printed sheet: «D. K. D. Vidensk. Selsk. Skr. 7. Række, hist. og filos. Afd. III. 1.», here «Skr. 7.» without the comma after «Skr.», on the left, and the sheet number «18» on the right; recorded here, not transcribed as a line.",
  "The table: rules and heads as on p. 136 (JP2 0168), with «cum veloci motu2)» for «Motus velox». Here each head is set from the top, one printed line to a line (L03-L09), the cells separated by our «|»; a head followed by empty cells spans their columns. The last row, 6s 0°, has 0 in every column of the values.",
  "L11-L40. Checked: the values for 150° + x are those for 30° − x of Tab. 21 (p. 132, JP2 0164) in reverse order, and 0 at 180°. They differ from Tab. 21 in sixteen places, seven of them by 1″ or 2″. Against the computation (as on p. 132): the equation of the sun agrees to within 1.1″ in all rows (with the readings of notes b-e); the equation of the moon to within 0.9″, except at 154°-156°, 158° and 159°; the declination to within 1.4″, except at 154°, 156°, 162°, 167°, 169° and 173°; the latitude to within 1.4″, except at 153°, 170° and 179°.",
  "The larger deviations. The moon at 155°, 2° 2′ 50″ against 2° 2′ 7″ computed and in Tab. 21 at 25°, 43″ more; at 154° and 159°, 2° 6′ 53″ and 1° 43′ 32″, the readings of C (notes g and h), where O's 43 and 22 give 2° 6′ 43″ and 1° 43′ 22″, the values of Tab. 21 at 26° and 21°, 0.3″ and 2.2″ from the computation. The declination at 156°, 9° 27′ 17″ against 9° 27′ 57″ (Tab. 21 at 24°), 40″ less; at 162°, 7° 10′ 50″ against 7° 10′ 40″ (Tab. 21 at 18°); at 167°, 5° 13′ 50″ against 5° 13′ 7″, the value that Tab. 21 also has at 13°; at 173°, 2° 49′ 22″, the 6″ deficit of Tab. 21 at 7°. The latitude at 170°, 0° 46′ 18″ against 0° 46′ 53″ (Tab. 21 at 10°), and at 179°, 0° 4′ 12″ against 0° 4′ 42″ (Tab. 21 at 1°), 35″ and 30″ less. No note of the apparatus bears on these, except g and h.",
  "The ellipses «. . . .» of the lemma as printed; «om.» in italics, the siglum C in roman."
 ],
